The `preprocess_fn` is a required user‑supplied function that prepares each batch of data before it is sent to the generator model. It is called once for every batch during the evaluation run, converting the raw batch into the inputs the model expects.

When the pipeline invokes this function it automatically supplies three arguments:

1. **`batch`** – a dictionary whose keys are the dataset field names and whose values are lists of the examples in the current batch (`dict[str, list]`);
2. **`rag`** – the RAG specification object for the leaf config (`RFLangChainRagSpec`);
3. **`prompt_manager`** – the prompt‑manager instance for that leaf config (`RFPromptManager`).

The function should return a dictionary of lists that will be used as the model’s inputs.
